<p>LEO dominates the orbital landscape at <strong>{leo_share}%</strong> of all active satellites. This is a direct consequence of the Starlink build-out and the broader trend toward LEO-based broadband constellations. The GEO belt, while far less populated numerically, carries a disproportionate share of high-throughput communications traffic. HEO is the smallest regime, used primarily for Molniya-class communications satellites serving high latitudes and specialized science missions.</p>

