  <li><strong>~97–99° cluster:</strong> Sun-synchronous orbit (SSO), used by Earth observation satellites (Planet, Spire, government imaging). The high density here reflects the commercial remote sensing boom.</li>
  <li><strong>~0–10° cluster:</strong> Equatorial and near-equatorial orbits, predominantly GEO satellites and some LEO equatorial constellations.</li>
  <li><strong>~63–65° cluster:</strong> Molniya-class HEO satellites and some navigation assets, providing coverage at high northern latitudes.</li>
