  <li><strong>{total - high_ecc_count:,} satellites ({100 - high_ecc_pct:.1f}%)</strong> have eccentricity below 0.01 — effectively circular orbits, dominated by LEO constellations and GEO communications satellites.</li>
  <li>Only <strong>{high_ecc_count} satellites ({high_ecc_pct}%)</strong> have eccentricities above 0.1. These include Molniya-class communications satellites (e ~0.7), highly elliptical science missions, and transfer-orbit objects.</li>
