<p>Within LEO, Starlink satellites cluster tightly around ~15.4–15.6 rev/day (corresponding to the ~530–550 km shell), while the broader LEO population spans from ~14.1 to ~16.5 rev/day, reflecting orbits from roughly 250 km to 1,600 km.</p>
